# Comments

**Canonical hard truth:** [`docs/comments.md`](../../docs/comments.md)

Write almost no comments — code and tests are the documentation. A comment-heavy file is a design
defect: extract a named function or write a named test instead of narrating. Comments earn their
place only for inherent complexity no decomposition removes, or business logic the code cannot
show (a constant's origin, an external quirk, a non-obvious invariant) — and they explain *why*.
Clean up narrating comments in any file you touch.
